Design notes
------------
- Payloads use compact SQL (no space after comma: `','` not `', '`) because the REAL
  nukesentinel.php get_ip() splits on `, ` for proxy chain handling. A `, ` inside the
  payload would fragment the injection across the comma handler.
- The 14-column INSERT (vs the old lifted 6-column version) requires 11 injected values.
  The subquery lands in the client_ip column (position 10).
- No blocker checks fire because nuke_nsnst_blockers table is empty, all config switches = 0.
- track_active=1 in nuke_nsnst_config is required for the tracked_ips INSERT to execute.

VERDICT: GENUINE incomplete-fix pair. gate_passed. Real NukeSentinel tarball code running
         against real MySQL, triggered by external HTTP.
